    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1000">

                <pb facs="0967" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.731/344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Göteborg</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sauer</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1000-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your despatch 83. You may transmit private commercial cables when no other means
                    available for forwarding, assuming no responsibility for delivery. Such cables
                    must be strictly neutral; not relate to contraband or transfer of funds to
                    belligerents; should be in plain language not cipher and sufficiently clear on
                    face to be readily understood. Cost should be collected in advance from
                    sender.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1000-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1000-f1-content">
                <p>The same to the Minister in the Netherlands, No. 112, February 26 (File No.
                    199.1/104).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
